1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,442
Teacher midterm practice, question 16.

2
00:00:04,062 --> 00:00:08,971
In Figure 1, the toughness can be approximated by the area bounded by which points?

3
00:00:10,670 --> 00:00:13,411
Toughness is the energy absorbed up to fracture:

4
00:00:13,411 --> 00:00:16,205
the area under the entire stress strain curve.

5
00:00:16,826 --> 00:00:19,130
The curve runs from O through B and D to

6
00:00:19,130 --> 00:00:25,119
fracture at F, and M is the strain at fracture. So the area is O, B, F, M.

7
00:00:26,719 --> 00:00:29,003
The answer is E: O, B, F, M.

8
00:00:29,822 --> 00:00:32,375
Do not stop the area at the tensile strength.

9
00:00:32,375 --> 00:00:35,026
Toughness counts all the energy up to fracture.
